WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.106 --> 00:00:23.089
Jean Valjean and Cosette walked for a while and then rode, changing carriages frequently as they headed toward

2
00:00:23.149 --> 00:00:28.211
Paris. The child did not complain even though she was exhausted.

3
00:00:28.811 --> 00:00:30.832
Finally Valjean picked her up.

4
00:00:31.488 --> 00:00:36.750
Without letting go of her doll, Cosette put her head on his shoulder and fell asleep.

5
00:00:37.551 --> 00:00:42.953
Valjean had rented rooms in a remote section of Paris, where they would not easily be spotted.

6
00:00:43.613 --> 00:00:49.996
The old Gorbeau house was a ruined dwelling, larger than it appeared from the street and mostly hidden

7
00:00:50.056 --> 00:00:50.536
from view.

8
00:00:51.397 --> 00:00:55.339
Valjean unlocked the door, which opened onto a steep staircase.

9
00:00:55.979 --> 00:01:01.846
The first floor of the building was a warehouse, and on the second floor were several run-down apartments.

10
00:01:02.686 --> 00:01:06.349
With another key, Valjean opened the door to his apartment.

11
00:01:06.889 --> 00:01:11.792
The first room was furnished with a mattress on the floor, a table, and some chairs.

12
00:01:12.752 --> 00:01:18.436
Beyond this room was a smaller one containing a cot, where Valjean laid Cosette without waking her.

13
00:01:19.777 --> 00:01:21.618
He bent down and kissed her hand.

14
00:01:22.258 --> 00:01:25.300
Nine months before, he had kissed her mother's hand.

15
00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:31.382
The next morning Valjean stood in the doorway watching Cosette, who was still sleeping.

16
00:01:32.143 --> 00:01:35.544
A cart rumbled down the street, and the noise woke her.

17
00:01:35.564 --> 00:01:37.625
"Yes, madame, I'm coming!"

18
00:01:38.005 --> 00:01:38.725
cried Cosette.

19
00:01:39.326 --> 00:01:41.867
She jumped out of bed, her eyes still half closed.

20
00:01:41.887 --> 00:01:45.028
"Oh, where's my broom?"

21
00:01:45.948 --> 00:01:51.451
Then she spotted the smiling face of Valjean, and realized she was no longer at the inn.

22
00:01:51.971 --> 00:01:54.612
She saw her doll, Catharine, at the foot of the bed.

23
00:01:55.644 --> 00:02:00.727
She picked up Catharine and played, all the while peppering Valjean with questions.

24
00:02:01.528 --> 00:02:02.368
Where was she?

25
00:02:02.968 --> 00:02:04.149
Was Paris a big place?

26
00:02:04.749 --> 00:02:07.091
Was Madame Thenardier really very far away?

27
00:02:07.571 --> 00:02:10.893
All at once Cosette exclaimed, "How pretty it is here!"

28
00:02:12.034 --> 00:02:17.417
She was living in rooms that were shabby and nearly bare, but to her this new home was

29
00:02:17.517 --> 00:02:22.520
beautiful. Yet it was difficult for her to shed her old routine.

30
00:02:23.404 --> 00:02:24.465
"Would you like me to sweep?"

31
00:02:24.805 --> 00:02:25.385
she asked.

32
00:02:25.405 --> 00:02:27.747
"No, you should play!"

33
00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:28.888
said Valjean.

34
00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:34.332
The next morning Valjean sat by Cosette's bed, waiting for her to wake.

35
00:02:34.952 --> 00:02:38.194
Something new was entering his soul: love.

36
00:02:39.075 --> 00:02:41.677
For so many years he had been alone in the world.

37
00:02:42.317 --> 00:02:45.439
His encounter with the bishop had led him to be more virtuous.

38
00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:52.124
Now Cosette was making him realize what it was like to love, and be loved.

39
00:02:53.024 --> 00:02:55.827
Cosette was also undergoing a metamorphosis.

40
00:02:56.467 --> 00:03:01.291
She had been so young when Fantine left her that she could not remember her mother.

41
00:03:02.252 --> 00:03:05.995
She had tried to love, but everyone at the inn had rejected her.

42
00:03:06.696 --> 00:03:12.260
So from the first day she met Valjean, she began to love her kind, old friend.

43
00:03:13.161 --> 00:03:16.164
Fate had brought together these two shattered beings.

44
00:03:16.844 --> 00:03:20.948
Cosette needed a father, just as Valjean needed a daughter.

45
00:03:22.456 --> 00:03:26.597
Weeks rolled by, and Valjean and Cosette lived happily together.

46
00:03:27.157 --> 00:03:28.718
He began teaching her to read.

47
00:03:29.738 --> 00:03:34.859
Often while working with her, he would remember that he had learned to read in prison with the

48
00:03:34.899 --> 00:03:36.420
intention of doing evil.

49
00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:41.161
Now his greatest joys were to teach Cosette and to watch her play.

50
00:03:41.781 --> 00:03:46.763
Sometimes he hoped that she would grow up to be ugly, so that no one would want to

51
00:03:46.823 --> 00:03:48.283
marry her and take her away.

52
00:03:48.883 --> 00:03:53.621
Meanwhile she addressed him as Father and knew him by no other name.

53
00:03:54.841 --> 00:03:58.562
Valjean still wore his threadbare yellow coat and tattered hat.

54
00:03:59.202 --> 00:04:05.744
On the street he was often mistaken for a beggar; sometimes kindhearted women even gave him money.

55
00:04:06.644 --> 00:04:09.705
Valjean always accepted their coins and bowed humbly.

56
00:04:10.305 --> 00:04:15.727
But if he happened to pass a poor creature begging, he would quickly look around and slip some

57
00:04:15.787 --> 00:04:17.307
change into the beggar's hand.

58
00:04:18.087 --> 00:04:22.617
Thus he began to be known in the neighborhood as "the generous beggar."

59
00:04:23.817 --> 00:04:27.239
Only one other person lived on the second floor of the Gorbeau house.

60
00:04:27.839 --> 00:04:32.021
That was the old woman who worked as the housekeeper and managed the building.

61
00:04:32.961 --> 00:04:38.303
She had rented the rooms to Valjean, who had passed himself off as a retired gentleman with a

62
00:04:38.343 --> 00:04:44.346
granddaughter. He had paid his rent six months in advance and said that he was living on his

63
00:04:44.406 --> 00:04:49.448
investments. The housekeeper was very curious about her unusual tenant.

64
00:04:49.948 --> 00:04:53.149
She watched him closely and quizzed Cosette about him.

65
00:04:53.889 --> 00:04:59.051
But she learned nothing until one day when she saw him go into one of the empty apartments,

66
00:04:59.531 --> 00:05:00.631
leaving the door open.

67
00:05:01.411 --> 00:05:05.773
The woman watched as he took scissors and ripped open the lapel of his coat.

68
00:05:06.453 --> 00:05:09.474
Then he removed a thousand-franc bank note!

69
00:05:10.294 --> 00:05:16.016
He soon asked her to get it changed for him, explaining that it was the six-month interest on

70
00:05:16.056 --> 00:05:16.756
his property.

71
00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:22.924
A few days later, when she was cleaning his room, she saw his coat lying on the floor.

72
00:05:24.285 --> 00:05:26.227
She picked it up and patted the lining.

73
00:05:26.747 --> 00:05:29.329
The coat felt as if it were padded with money!

74
00:05:30.209 --> 00:05:33.932
Meanwhile Valjean never left the apartment before twilight.

75
00:05:34.533 --> 00:05:39.797
His evening walks often took him past a church, where he gave money to an old beggar.

76
00:05:40.917 --> 00:05:44.160
One night Valjean put a coin in the man's hand as usual.

77
00:05:44.768 --> 00:05:48.711
The beggar suddenly raised his eyes and looked intently at his benefactor.

78
00:05:49.511 --> 00:05:53.214
Valjean pulled back, horror-stricken, as the man looked away.

79
00:05:53.814 --> 00:05:57.177
The beggar looked just like Javert!

80
00:05:57.197 --> 00:06:00.919
"Surely I'm mistaken," Valjean said to himself.

81
00:06:00.939 --> 00:06:02.820
"I must get another look at him."

82
00:06:03.821 --> 00:06:06.583
The next night Valjean looked for the beggar again.

83
00:06:06.603 --> 00:06:07.784
"Good evening!"

84
00:06:08.104 --> 00:06:10.145
said Valjean, handing the man a coin.

85
00:06:10.165 --> 00:06:13.568
"Thank you, kind sir," replied the beggar.

86
00:06:14.372 --> 00:06:17.433
Valjean was relieved to recognize the face of the beggar.

87
00:06:17.453 --> 00:06:23.735
"My eyesight must be getting poor," he said to himself and thought no more about it.

88
00:06:24.695 --> 00:06:29.817
A few nights later, he was helping Cosette with her spelling when he heard someone coming up the

89
00:06:29.857 --> 00:06:34.138
stairs. It was late enough that he knew the housekeeper was already in bed.

90
00:06:34.978 --> 00:06:39.019
He made a sign for Cosette to be silent, and then blew out his candle.

91
00:06:39.619 --> 00:06:44.469
Sitting still in his chair, he listened as the footsteps stopped in front of his door.

92
00:06:45.529 --> 00:06:48.410
He could see the light of a candle shining through the keyhole.

93
00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:52.691
Someone was standing outside his door and listening.

94
00:06:53.391 --> 00:06:55.952
Several minutes later the person walked away.

95
00:06:56.912 --> 00:06:58.393
Valjean sent Cosette to bed.

96
00:06:58.873 --> 00:07:03.274
He threw himself on his bed without undressing, but he could not sleep that night.

97
00:07:04.174 --> 00:07:07.515
The next morning he heard the same footsteps in the hallway.

98
00:07:08.055 --> 00:07:11.156
He tiptoed from his bed and peered through the keyhole.

99
00:07:11.996 --> 00:07:16.598
As the man reached the stairs, he turned and Valjean saw his profile.

100
00:07:18.279 --> 00:07:19.459
It was Javert!

101
00:07:20.099 --> 00:07:21.880
Who had given him a key to the building?

102
00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:23.381
Why was he here?

103
00:07:24.121 --> 00:07:28.203
When the housekeeper came to sweep Valjean's room, he asked her no questions.

104
00:07:28.943 --> 00:07:33.425
But she said, "Perhaps monsieur heard someone arriving last night?

105
00:07:34.265 --> 00:07:35.365
It was the new tenant."

106
00:07:35.386 --> 00:07:41.268
"Oh yes, I thought I heard someone on the stairs," he said as casually as possible.

107
00:07:41.824 --> 00:07:42.404
"Who is he?"

108
00:07:42.424 --> 00:07:48.147
"Monsieur Dumont, a gentleman living on his investments like you."

109
00:07:49.387 --> 00:07:54.390
That night Valjean went out the front door and looked carefully up and down the street.

110
00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:57.211
Then he went upstairs again.

111
00:07:57.231 --> 00:08:00.633
"Come," he said as he took Cosette's hand.

112
00:08:00.653 --> 00:08:02.533
"We must leave this place."
